      "content": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 1
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Abstract"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This example follows the Darcy-flow problem in Fourier Neural Operator and brings together the original paper, author-maintained code, a public small dataset and an editable manuscript. The figure displays reference data packaged with the repository. This run reads, checks and plots the data; it does not train an FNO."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 1
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1. Research question"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Parametric partial differential equations require repeated solutions for different input fields. FNO learns a mapping from an input function to a solution function and parameterizes an integral kernel in Fourier space. The Darcy-flow example maps a spatially varying coefficient field to a steady-state solution [1]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 1
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "2. Equation and conditions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockMath",
          "attrs": {
            "latex": "-\\nabla\\cdot(a(x)\\nabla u(x))=1,\\quad x\\in(0,1)^2"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "blockMath",
          "attrs": {
            "latex": "u(x)=0,\\quad x\\in\\partial(0,1)^2"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "These conditions follow Appendix A.3.2 of the downloaded FNO paper. In the original paper, the coefficient takes two positive values, and reference solutions are computed on a 421 × 421 grid before downsampling. This workspace uses the small example file in the current NeuralOperator repository and does not equate it with the complete original benchmark."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 1
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "3. Data and figure"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The current file stores the input phase as torch.bool. The left panel shows the stored 0/1 encoding directly, and the right panel shows the associated reference target. The binary values are not presented as permeability values with physical units, and no unverified encoding map is reconstructed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "attrs": {
            "src": "asset:darcy-reference.png",
            "title": "Figure 1. A small Darcy test sample from NeuralOperator: stored binary input encoding and associated reference target.",
            "alt": "Stored Darcy phase encoding and reference target"
          }
        },
