        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 1
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "4. What validation should establish"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Organizing sources and validating a predictive model serve different purposes. The present output checks whether files, images and program references agree. Training experiments should report errors on independent test samples and specify training resolution, testing resolution and normalization. The PINO reference [2] supports an examination of physical constraints, while DeepONet [3] provides a different operator representation for comparison."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 1
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "5. Running the example and its sources"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Run python src/plot_reference.py from the program folder to regenerate Figure 1. The author-maintained training example is src/plot_FNO_darcy.py, and src/fno.py contains the model implementation from the same commit. Full training requires the upstream NeuralOperator environment. The local copy is pinned to a6648eeeb60fe0837f2d7d021517a945a159a0c8 and retains the MIT license. The figure was generated by a Slurm job on the registered research cluster."
            }
          ]
        },
